node_modules/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored, `coverage/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth - and it did: dist/coverage/index.html
# is the site's public Coverage Map, linked from 559 built pages and listed in
# sitemap-pages.xml, and git refused to track it. Every build wrote it, no
# commit could keep it, and validate:generated-surfaces, validate:links and
# validate:public-surfaces failed on every fresh checkout of main. Nobody saw
# it because validate:all builds before it validates. Same reasoning for tmp/.
/coverage/
/tmp/
.DS_Store
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
